    "36 app.commandLine behavior: existing code appends switches, no commandLine replacement.",
    "37 utilityProcess behavior: owned Node worker_threads and child processes remain the used paths; settings worker and native process/session cases passed.",
    "38/44 platform removals: local evidence Windows x64 only; no ia32 release claimed, no macOS/Linux native run.",
    "39 window.open defaults: app/webview popup denial and source gates retained, real foreign-frame/navigation tests passed.",
    "40/44 clipboard: first-party writes remain in main; awaited IPC completion/rejection and tray error handling covered with controlled promises.",
    "41 PDF behavior and 43 native dialog defaults: no PDF-specific lifecycle assumptions added; native picker UX remains a manual acceptance condition.",
    "42 runtime download: explicit install preparation before CI verification; exact binary acquired and all current native checks use 44.9.0.",
    "44 ANGLE static linkage: no app-managed EGL/GLES DLL replacement; actual default-GPU window and packaged mpv frame smoke succeeded."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Native clipboard contents were neither read nor written; async behavior tested with controlled promises at actual production handlers.",
    "Source hidden-window capture initially failed UnknownVizError; inactive visible capture succeeded and was inspected.",
    "Initial packaged metadata preload was unsupported, so the first owned QA process was stopped after timeout; final CDP/portable checks succeeded and exited normally.",
    "ASAR reader initially used POSIX separators for deep Windows paths; native paths resolved the tool lookup and all selected shipped sources matched.",
    "Directory build disables signing and branding edits and publishes nothing. No NSIS/portable installer, signature or coverage-install acceptance.",
    "Five-second generated silent H264 and one decoded frame are a smoke check, not all codecs, hardware decode proof, sustained frame/latency/memory budgets or real mobile playback.",
    "Vite, electron-builder, mobile runtime/native modules, remaining tooling vulnerabilities, migration/other stores, release manifests/signing and TLS work remain open.",
    "Core/release CI gates updated and inspected; remote CI jobs were not dispatched."
  ]
